module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.TenGap
public import Rule30Open.Columns.ElevenTraps
public import Rule30Open.Columns.TwelveTraps

/-!
# Right halves white past their first eight cells enter the walls of `00000011011` and `001011100111`

[TenGap](TenGap.md) shows that no finite configuration whose cells 9 to 3,058 are white has a center column that
repeats `0000010001`, from the entries of the 2,560 halves of at most eight cells into its wall. The same holds for
the walls of period 11 and 12 that [ElevenTraps](ElevenTraps.md) and [TwelveTraps](TwelveTraps.md) carry: every half of
at most eight cells enters the wall of `00000011011` by step 1,594 and that of `001011100111` by step 2,341, from every
phase, and the white half by steps 664 and 836.

* `eleven_gap`, `eleven_white`: `00000011011`, with cells 9 to 1,610 white, or cells 1 to 680.
* `twelve_gap`, `twelve_white`: `001011100111`, with cells 9 to 2,357 white, or cells 1 to 852.

The natural-language argument is `WallGaps.md`, beside this file. The entries come from
`python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-wall-gaps`.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata BitGame
open Rule30Ether Rule30EtherThree Rule30Realization Rule30PeriodTwoSideways

